{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488781-play-the-rio-de-janeiro-atmosphere","id":1488781,"title":"Play the Rio de Janeiro atmosphere","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-02T03:41:10-07:00","id":1488781,"title":"Play the Rio de Janeiro atmosphere","content":"Hi everyone, I open this topic for a series of tips.<br /> My gaming group and I discovered the city of Rio de Janeiro from the canon and we found it extremely interesting, especially for the &quot;shared&quot; government between Camarilla and Sabbat and that open city aspect it seems to have.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to inform myself as much as possible about the city so as not to reduce it to the stereotyped idea of &quot;outdoor brothel, transsexuals, carnival and Pele's t-shirts&quot; as someone said on the forum and I was wondering if anyone who visited it or who lives can you tell me something more about its atmosphere and maybe about any plots or ideas that you can bring to the game table.<br /> <br /> I ask for this advice with the fear of raising a fuss given the accusations of cultural appropriation, stereotyping that he saw in the forum and commented myself, and that I understand as an Italian (yes, we are all mafia and very Catholic! XD), so have pity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T12:08:42-07:00","id":1488862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488781-play-the-rio-de-janeiro-atmosphere#post1488781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi everyone, I open this topic for a series of tips.<br /> My gaming group and I discovered the city of Rio de Janeiro from the canon and we found it extremely interesting, especially for the &amp;quot;shared&amp;quot; government between Camarilla and Sabbat and that open city aspect it seems to have.<br /> <br /> I'm trying to inform myself as much as possible about the city so as not to reduce it to the stereotyped idea of &amp;quot;outdoor brothel, transsexuals, carnival and Pele's t-shirts&amp;quot; as someone said on the forum and I was wondering if anyone who visited it or who lives can you tell me something more about its atmosphere and maybe about any plots or ideas that you can bring to the game table.<br /> <br /> I ask for this advice with the fear of raising a fuss given the accusations of cultural appropriation, stereotyping that he saw in the forum and commented myself, and that I understand as an Italian (yes, we are all mafia and very Catholic! XD), so have pity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did find the official canon?<br /> I was in Rio only for 10 days but I fell in love with the city. It's a city with many contrasts and surprises","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T12:42:09-07:00","id":1488869,"title":"","content":"Hi fellow italian! <br /> <br /> Grab this fan made manual from the Storytellers Vault, it's fantastic and writte by a local: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/261806\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/261806</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T20:13:15-07:00","id":1488926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Querion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488781-play-the-rio-de-janeiro-atmosphere#post1488781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm trying to inform myself as much as possible about the city so as not to reduce it to the stereotyped idea of &quot;outdoor brothel, transsexuals, carnival and Pele's t-shirts&quot; as someone said on the forum and I was wondering if anyone who visited it or who lives can you tell me something more about its atmosphere and maybe about any plots or ideas that you can bring to the game table.<br /> <br /> I ask for this advice with the fear of raising a fuss given the accusations of cultural appropriation, stereotyping that he saw in the forum and commented myself, and that I understand as an Italian (yes, we are all mafia and very Catholic! XD), so have pity.</div> </div> </div> </div>My father's family is from Rio and I've been there several times.<br /> <br /> For one thing, people using light clothes most of the time is perfectly normal, and while most people <b>won't </b>be doing it, at any time and any place you may come across someone on swimming clothes. The city has many beaches, for all social classes, and it is really hot in summer, so that's kind of a survival thing (some people still go about on heavy clothes, they're aliens, I'm 100% sure).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it is maybe as heavily Catholic as Rome itself or more. So nothing as extreme as small towns really manage to be, but still it isn't at all like a brothel. Every year several foreign tourists assume the light clothes and skimpy swimming clothes (they're real and popular, but not the only thing going around) indicate the legends are true, just to end up in jail for indecent behavior or even assault when they try to act like naturists. Some beaches do let a woman go topless nowadays, but that'll <b>never</b> fly about without a lot of shocked looks.<br /> <br /> Transsexuals aren't going around free as birds, either, only if they have a death wish. During Carnival transgender costumes are popular (not the most popular, but certainly very popular), specially for men to dress as women (the opposite is far less common. Misogyny? You can bet), and most aren't actual transgenders. The rest of the years you'll have the usual of any big city, transgender people trying to live in peace and frequently at a low profile, and some more openly transgender working at Red Light districts at night, trying to make a living and survive the combined hate against sex workers and gays. Things like the Gay Parade in Brazil happen in another city, at another state, S\u00e3o Paulo.<br /> <br /> Carnival is a big affair, but it is once a year. We actually have other places in the country that look nothing like Rio de Janeiro and have far more Carnival-related or Carnival-like festivities. For the rest of the year, just no, there's no such a thing.<br /> <br /> No one even remembers Pel\u00e9 most of the time, but Football is certainly a huge thing. Most people like it, and even those who don't are expected to have a team of choice. Like, not cheering to anyone is actually weirder than just not liking the sport. In fact people love to exhibit the shield and colors of their team, and you'll see from rich girls with a small team shield jewelry pending from their expensive bags and their socialite mothers using it as some other subtle jewelry, to people that have everything adorned in homage to their teams, clothes, car, mug, bedroom, dog, everything. My uncle Claudio's house was almost completely black and white with red Da Gama crosses all over the place (the colors and symbol of his Vasco Da Gama team). While old people may remember with great nostalgia of the players of yore and what they see as a more artistic Football, most people will discuss current players.<br /> <br /> People in Rio talk with a slow accent even for Brazillian standards, and we already have a slow accent in comparison with almost anyone.Their accent have a cadence to it and a way of coming out that I can't quite describe except as being almost as half-singing, although it has no pitch accent to it, just the usual stress accent. For many Brazilians it sounds a lot as a con-man, to be honest, but I really find it a beautiful accent.<br /> <br /> As my parting words for now, I'd like to make the place's climate and geography clearer. Despite being known for the heat, it is actually fairly in the south of the Tropical Region and most neighboring places have a climate more similar to temperate. What happens is that its location works almost like a natural pressure cooker, the city lies between a bay and a range of mountains that traps the hot, humid air inside a giant bubble. As a result, summer temperatures easily raise above 40\u00baC (105 \u00baF) and can be as high as 45 (113), sometimes even higher. In winter it is still higher than 20 or 21 (70) most of the time, but for many Cariocas this is more than enough to put on a coat, no joke, some even rattle teeth at this point (I personally find it quite pleasurable and can barely survive there in summer). Some other cities exist in the same general area between the bay and the mountains. The most popular retreat outside the city, though, is Petr\u00f3polis, a mountain city that used to be the Imperial Summer Residence, and has a far colder climate (obviously).<br /> <br /> Just some random bits about the city. I can give more and some for other places in Brazil if you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  Some glaring typos... but hey, I AM Brazilian, my first language is Portuguese. 08-04-2022, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T22:10:32-07:00","id":1488938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488781-play-the-rio-de-janeiro-atmosphere?p=1488862#post1488862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where did find the official canon?<br /> I was in Rio only for 10 days but I fell in love with the city. It's a city with many contrasts and surprises</div> </div> </div> </div>It all started from the wiki, then I looked for information on the vampire situation in various sites and we got an idea that we could mod.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26315-querion","name":"Querion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-02T22:11:22-07:00","id":1488939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488781-play-the-rio-de-janeiro-atmosphere?p=1488869#post1488869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi fellow italian!<br /> <br /> Grab this fan made manual from the Storytellers Vault, it's fantastic and writte by a local: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/261806\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/m/product/261806</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hello to you, I'll try to check it out as soon as I can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2